title: Eviction_Under_Door
---
<<declare $seen_eviction = false>>
<<if $seen_eviction == false>>
	The corner of a folded envelope sticks out from beneath the front door. 
	She crouches and pulls it free, unfolding it carefully to avoid making a noise.
	<<start_character_conv CharacterManager "Ashe">>
	Ashe: An Eviction Notice?
	<<show_evidence GameManager "Eviction Letter">>
	Her eyes move over the words, then back to the top of the page, as if reading it a second time might somehow change what it says. The paper trembles slightly between her fingers.
	Behind her, her father sleeps on the couch, one arm hanging over the edge, his face slack with exhaustion. 
	The television murmurs in the background, washing the dim living room in the pale morning light.

	She glances at him, waiting for him to stir. He doesn't.
	<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Ashe" "sad">>
	For a moment, she remains crouched by the door, the notice resting against her knees. Her expression tightens as the reality of the situation settles in. 
	She presses her lips together, folds the paper along its original creases and slips it into her pocket.
	<<hide_evidence GameManager>>
	<<show_character_expression CharacterManager "Ashe" "default">>
	Then she stands and looks around the apartment\: the worn carpet, the peeling wallpaper, the familiar clutter that has always made the place feel like home, despite everything.

	Her father shifts in his sleep, muttering something unintelligible.

	She turns toward him, the eviction notice heavy in her pocket, and quietly closes her eyes. There is no point waking him. 

	Not yet, not whilst she needs to grab his medication from his room. The one he just refuses to use now.
	<<hide_evidence GameManager>>
	<<obtain_evidence GameManager "Eviction Letter">>
	You got Eviction Letter. 
	<<set $seen_eviction = true>>
	<<allow_travel GameManager>>
<<else>>
	...
	No point looking at it again
<<endif>>
<<end_character_conv CharacterManager>>
===

